From 3c32b7989d974afe435b9332253cf32cef64524e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:37:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(properties): order listing by launch date, newest
 first

Projects with a readable launch_date lead the /properties listing, most
recent first; the 33 without one keep their existing relative order
behind them. We deliberately do not fall back to the WordPress publish
date, because every property was entered during the mid-2026 bulk import
and that date records data entry, not launch.

launch_date is a free-text ACF field, so src/lib/launchDate.ts parses the
shapes editors actually use (11 September 2025, October 2024, 2025, ISO,
stray whitespace) and sorts on whatever date it can find. It prints a
'Launched Oct 2025' line on the card only when the whole value is a clean
date, so a prose value like ACE Arte's ('RERA registered July 2026,
allotment expected around 10 August 2026') still sorts but never renders
an allotment date as a launch date.

Also raises the /properties fetch from 50 to 100. There are 54 projects
in WordPress, so four were silently invisible - including two 2026
launches.

Verified against all 21 real launch_date values on production via
scripts/verify-launch-sort.ts.
