From ef4e2dc92402a19eacc332475d04bcbcd22f543e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:37:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(properties): add Pre-Launch section driven by an
 explicit flag
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Projects an editor has flagged with is_prelaunch, and which carry no RERA
number, render in their own band below the main listing. Cards show a
PRE-LAUNCH badge, the editor's expected_launch text in place of a launch
date, 'Price on Request' instead of a figure, and a Register Interest CTA.

The flag must be explicit. A blank rera_number does NOT imply pre-launch:
four projects have no RERA number in WordPress today and two of them
(ACE Golfshire, ACE Platinum) are Ready to Move, so inferring the state
from a blank would advertise finished towers as unlaunched.

The RERA number overrides the flag in the other direction, which is the
promotion the business wants — entering a number returns the project to
the main listing on the next revalidate regardless of the checkbox, so
data entry cannot strand a registered project in pre-launch.

Pre-launch obeys location, type and budget filters but not the status
chips: 'Ready to Move' and 'Under Construction' describe registered
construction stages an unregistered project cannot answer, so selecting
any status hides the section rather than guessing.

Requires two new ACF fields on the properties CPT (is_prelaunch true/false,
expected_launch text). Until they exist the section never renders.
